// REPRODUCED (semantics-v2-subtype-rules, ruling 2026-10-10). The [CR#301.5]
// host rule is the deontic "this Equipment may be attached to a creature" over
// the attach deed's host role [CR#701.3a], conferred ability-free as
// `Property`; the [CR#704.5n] state-based action is "if it isn't attached to a
// legal host, it becomes unattached". Legality is the engine's attach-permission
// model under default-deny, so the condition reads the attachment relation the
// model keeps, and an Equipment attached to nothing is already unattached
// [CR#701.3d]; no `legallyAttached` primitive is written.
//
// The v1 core type-rule record this declaration carried until
// `plugins-v2-subtypes-macro-only`, preserved verbatim so nothing is lost:
//
//     body: Subtype(
//         name: "Equipment",
//         types: [Artifact],
//         confers: [
//             Static(May(attach(what: Ref(This), to: Type(Creature)))),
//         ],
//     ),
//
// Equipment ([CR#301.5]) — "an Equipment can be attached to a creature. It
// can't legally be attached to anything that isn't a creature." That STATES A
// QUALITY of the object, which [CR#113.12] is explicit is neither granting an
// ability nor setting a characteristic, so the host rule is conferred
// ability-free as the `Static` flavor rather than forged into an Ability.
Subtype(
    category: Artifact,
    name: "equipment",
    spelling: "Equipment",
    grammar: Noun(singular: "Equipment", plural: "Equipment"),
    params: [],
    rules: [
        Property(mayBeAttachedTo(thisEquipment, allOf(creature))),
        StateBased(
            not(matches(thisEquipment, attachment(Attachment))),
            attachment(Unattached, thisEquipment),
        ),
    ],
)
